fix(ai-operator): init containers are PodSecurity-restricted compliant

The operator pod was rejected by PSA "restricted" (namespace enforce) because
the `tools` and `deps` initContainers ran as runAsUser=0 -> "0 replicas updated".

- tools: use busybox wget/tar from base alpine instead of `apk add` -> no root
- deps:  pip install --target needs no root; HOME=/tmp, PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR
- code:  git config safe.directory, HOME=/tmp
- all init containers now inherit the pod's runAsUser 65532 / runAsNonRoot /
  drop-ALL / seccomp; readOnlyRootFilesystem dropped on init only (not required
  by restricted; pip/git/wget need a writable /)
- deps container verifies imports (kopf, kubernetes, httpx, numpy, yaml)

Also:
- external-Ollama reachability check now runs a properly-secured Pod (the old
  `kubectl run` was itself PSA-rejected in the restricted namespace) and prints
  a concrete bind/firewall/routing checklist on failure
- rollout wait 300s -> 420s + dumps pod state & events on timeout

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
